  "note": "Lean never uses the pure Gaussian: η₊ = h_H(t)te^{−t²/2} goes through the k = 2 bound shifted to s − 1 (Explicit/EtaPlusMellin), and η_* through Mellin convolution with t²e^{−t²/2}. So the k = 0 and k = 1 cases of Cor 8.0.2 are not needed."
